871 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart with fifteen numbered black circles connected in a winding path, each representing a step in a course sequence. Each step lists a module name, such as \215The Awakening,\216 \215The Debugging Challenge,\216 and \215The Final Reboot,\216 along with tutorial topics and subjects including Operating Systems, Fundamentals of Databases, Computer Architecture, Computer Networking, Cyber-Physical Systems, and Linear Algebra. The path visually guides progression through the modules, culminating at \215The Open Campus\216 for exploration.) /K 924 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 285 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
872 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart detailing a virtual reality conversational AI system across five phases: user initiation, audio capture, language model processing, response synthesis, and playback, showing components like Unreal Engine, speech recognition, large language model, text-to-speech, phoneme analysis, and NPC avatar presentation with labeled arrows indicating data flow.) /K 925 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 287 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
873 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart showing two phases for VR implementation. Phase 1 involves Unreal Engine 5 \(desktop\), VaRest Plugin \(REST API/JSON\), OpenAI API \(GPT-3.5\) for text LLM, with keyboard typing as input. Phase 2 involves Unreal Engine 5 \(VR mode\), Convai Plugin as unified AI platform integrating STT, LLM, TTS, and lip-sync, Ready Player Me for 3D avatars, and input from voice and push-to-talk.) /K 926 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 288 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
874 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Humanoid robot statue stands outdoors with outstretched arms against a partly cloudy sky, positioned in front of a dark, modern building. Overlayed text in white and purple provides an introduction from Akira Johnson, an Information Engineering student, and explains the significance of the D-Building at Technical University of Munich Campus Heilbronn.) /K 927 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 289 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
875 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart depicting a voice interaction system with labeled boxes: VR Headset Mic \(User Speech\) connects to STT API \(Speech-to-Text\), which provides a User Transcript to the LLM API \(OpenAI via VaRest Plugin\). LLM API outputs Response Text to TTS API \(Text-to-Speech\), generating Audio Output for the Lip-Sync Module, which synchronizes animation for an NPC Character \(3D Model\). Labels indicate the process at each connection, including \215Audio Stream\216, \215User Transcript\216, \215Response Text\216, \215Audio Output\216, and \215Output with Animation\216.) /K 928 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 291 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
876 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart-style Unreal Engine Blueprint visual scripting shows the EnhancedInputAction IA_Talk node with two output pins, Started and Completed, connected to Start Talking and Stop Talking nodes respectively, both targeting Convai Base Player.) /K 929 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 292 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
877 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Screenshot of a character creation interface showing a highlighted \215Character Description\216 tab on the left with other options such as Avatar, Language and Speech, Knowledge Bank, and Core AI Settings, each segmented and numbered from one to three. On the right, fields labeled Character\220s Name and Character\220s ID are displayed, with details for a character named Akira Johnson, a twenty-one-year-old American student at TUM Campus Heilbronn, and a brief biography describing her academic background and activities.) /K 930 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 293 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
878 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar chart comparing completion rates for three tasks: Information Retrieval \(Task A\) at ninety-six percent, Navigation \(Task B\) at one hundred percent, and Language Practice \(Task C\) at eighty-three percent.) /K 931 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 297 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
879 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bar chart showing UEQ scores for six categories: Attractiveness, Perspicuity, Efficiency, Dependability, Stimulation, and Novelty. Stimulation and Novelty have the highest mean values around two, while Dependability is lowest. Error bars indicate variability.) /K 932 0 R /P 303 0 R /Pg 297 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
